---
import StandardPageLayout from "../../layouts/StandardPageLayout.astro";
import PageToc from "../../components/PageToc.astro";
import LifecycleNotice from "../../components/StandardLifecycleNotice.astro";
import "../../styles/standards-poster.css";
import "../../styles/extended.css";
import metadata from "../../data/standards/japangaap/asbj37.json";
---

<StandardPageLayout
  code={metadata.code}
  standardType={metadata.framework}
  title={metadata.title}
  description={metadata.summary}
  issued={metadata.issued}
  latestAmendment={metadata.latestAmendment}
  status={metadata.status}
  summary={metadata.summary}
>
  <Fragment slot="toc">
    <PageToc
      items={[
        { id: "s1", label: "Conceptual Framework Linkage" },
        { id: "s2", label: "Scope — the Current Statutory Interim Reporting Standard" },
        { id: "s3", label: "What Changed From Statement No. 33" },
        { id: "s4", label: "Minimum Content of an Interim Report" },
        { id: "s5", label: "The Coordinated Reform Package — No. 37 Through No. 40" },
        { id: "s6", label: "Worked Example — Interim Reporting Under the Current Standard" },
        { id: "s7", label: "Disclosure Requirements" },
        { id: "s8", label: "Critical Judgments & Estimates" },
        { id: "s9", label: "Relationship to IAS/IFRS" },
        { id: "s10", label: "Statement Mapping" },
        { id: "s11", label: "Related Standards" },
        { id: "s12", label: "Glossary" },
      ]}
    />
  </Fragment>

  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="callout info callout--centered">RECENCY NOTE: Issued October 16, 2025, alongside a coordinated package of related standards (No. 38, 39, and 40 — see companion posters). As current, recently-issued material, details should be cross-checked against ASBJ's own published materials for any subsequent refinement.</div>

    <div class="toc">
      <a href="#s1">1. Conceptual Framework Linkage</a>
      <a href="#s2">2. Scope — the Current Statutory Interim Reporting Standard</a>
      <a href="#s3">3. What Changed From Statement No. 33</a>
      <a href="#s4">4. Minimum Content of an Interim Report</a>
      <a href="#s5">5. The Coordinated Reform Package — No. 37 Through No. 40</a>
      <a href="#s6">6. Worked Example — Interim Reporting Under the Current Standard</a>
      <a href="#s7">7. Disclosure Requirements</a>
      <a href="#s8">8. Critical Judgments &amp; Estimates</a>
      <a href="#s9">9. Relationship to IAS/IFRS</a>
      <a href="#s10">10. Statement Mapping</a>
      <a href="#s11">11. Related Standards</a>
      <a href="#s12">12. Glossary</a>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s1">
      <span class="num">1</span>
      <h2>Conceptual Framework Linkage</h2>
      <span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card ci span2">
        <div class="ctitle ci">The current, refined successor to Japan's 2024 semi-annual reporting reform</div>
        <div class="principle">ASBJ Statement No. 37 REWORKS and REPLACES ASBJ Statement No. 33 (Semi-annual Financial Reporting, 2024 — see the companion poster), renaming and REFINING Japan's CURRENT statutory interim reporting framework as "Interim Financial Reporting" — issued as PART of a COORDINATED package alongside three related amendment Statements (No. 38, 39, and 40).</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s2">
      <span class="num">2</span>
      <h2>Scope — the Current Statutory Interim Reporting Standard</h2>
      <span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cw span2">
        <div class="ctitle cw">Listed companies' interim (second-quarter) reporting obligation</div>
        <div class="principle">This Statement applies to LISTED companies preparing their STATUTORY interim (second fiscal quarter) financial report — the CURRENT primary interim reporting obligation, REPLACING both the OLD full quarterly regime (ASBJ Statement No. 12) and its immediate PREDECESSOR, the 2024 semi-annual standard (ASBJ Statement No. 33).</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s3">
      <span class="num">3</span>
      <h2>What Changed From Statement No. 33</h2>
      <span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2">
        <div class="ctitle cd">Renaming and refinement following initial implementation experience</div>
        <div class="text-supporting">
          <div style="font-size:11px;color:var(--color-text-secondary);line-height:1.6;">The SHIFT in TERMINOLOGY — from "SEMI-ANNUAL Financial Reporting" to "INTERIM Financial Reporting" — REFLECTS more than a simple RENAME; it accompanied a COORDINATED set of REFINEMENTS addressing PRACTICAL implementation questions that arose FOLLOWING the 2024 rollout, INCLUDING companion amendments to consolidated semi-annual statement PREPARATION (No. 38), consolidated cash flow statement preparation (No. 39), and tax effect accounting for INTERIM purposes (No. 40) — TOGETHER forming a genuinely COORDINATED reform package RATHER than an isolated standard revision.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s4">
      <span class="num">4</span>
      <h2>Minimum Content of an Interim Report</h2>
      <span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cs span2">
        <div class="ctitle cs">A condensed set of statements, consistent with general interim principles</div>
        <div class="text-supporting">
          <div style="font-size:11px;color:var(--color-text-secondary);line-height:1.6;">A COMPLIANT interim report includes a CONDENSED Balance Sheet, condensed Statement of Income, condensed Statement of Changes in Net Assets, condensed Statement of Cash Flows, and SELECTED explanatory notes — CONSISTENT with the general interim reporting principles ESTABLISHED under J-GAAP (materiality assessed relative to the interim period, same accounting policies as the annual accounts).</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s5">
      <span class="num">5</span>
      <h2>The Coordinated Reform Package — No. 37 Through No. 40</h2>
      <span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cw span2">
        <div class="ctitle cw">Four related Statements issued together on the same date</div>
        <div class="td-table">
          <div class="th cols-06-24">
            <span>Statement</span>
            <span>Role</span>
          </div>
          <div class="tr cols-06-24">
            <span>No. 37</span>
            <span>THIS Statement — the general Interim Financial Reporting framework</span>
          </div>
          <div class="tr alt cols-06-24">
            <span>No. 38</span>
            <span>Partial Amendments to the Preparation of Semi-annual CONSOLIDATED Financial Statements — see the companion poster</span>
          </div>
          <div class="tr cols-06-24">
            <span>No. 39</span>
            <span>Partial Amendments to Preparing Consolidated Statements of CASH FLOWS (Part 3) — see the companion poster</span>
          </div>
          <div class="tr alt cols-06-24">
            <span>No. 40</span>
            <span>Partial Amendments to TAX EFFECT ACCOUNTING (Part 2) — see the companion poster</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s6">
      <span class="num">6</span>
      <h2>Worked Example — Interim Reporting Under the Current Standard</h2>
      <span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cw span2">
        <div class="ctitle cw">A condensed report under the current framework</div>
        <div class="worked worked--flush">
          <div class="wk-title">Example: A listed company's current interim filing cycle</div>
          <div class="wk-body">A listed company prepares its second-quarter statutory interim report under the CURRENT ASBJ Statement No. 37 framework.</div>
          <div class="wk-answer">The report includes a CONDENSED set of primary financial statements and SELECTED notes, applying the SAME accounting policies as the ANNUAL accounts, with MATERIALITY assessed relative to the SIX-MONTH interim period — CONSISTENT with the GENERAL interim reporting principles carried FORWARD from the earlier ASBJ Statement No. 33, now REFINED under this current standard.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s7">
      <span class="num">7</span>
      <h2>Disclosure Requirements</h2>
      <span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2">
        <div class="ctitle cd">What ASBJ Statement No. 37 requires</div>
        <div class="check-list">
          <span>Condensed primary financial statements for the interim period</span>
          <span>Selected explanatory notes on significant events and transactions since the last annual report</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s8">
      <span class="num">8</span>
      <h2>Critical Judgments &amp; Estimates</h2>
      <span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cn span2">
        <div class="ctitle cn">Where judgement matters most</div>
        <div class="two-col">
          <div>
            <div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT JUDGEMENTS</div>
            <div class="dot-list">
              <span>Materiality assessment relative to the interim period</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div>
            <div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT ESTIMATES</div>
            <div class="dot-list">
              <span>Interim-period tax effect estimates, coordinated with the companion ASBJ Statement No. 40 amendments</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s9">
      <span class="num">9</span>
      <h2>Relationship to IAS/IFRS</h2>
      <span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card ci span2">
        <div class="ctitle ci">Comparison — J-GAAP vs IAS 34</div>
        <div class="text-supporting">
          <div style="font-size:11px;color:var(--color-text-secondary);line-height:1.6;">As with its PREDECESSOR standards, IAS 34's OWN principles (condensed statements, consistent accounting policies, interim-period materiality) remain BROADLY applicable REGARDLESS of the SPECIFIC reporting frequency a jurisdiction adopts — Japan's REFINED interim reporting framework CONTINUES to reflect these SAME general principles, now UNDER a renamed and REFINED statutory structure.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s10">
      <span class="num">10</span>
      <h2>Statement Mapping</h2>
      <span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cs span2">
        <div class="ctitle cs">Where every interim reporting event lands</div>
        <div class="td-table">
          <div class="th cols-16-1-14">
            <span>Event</span>
            <span>Statement(s) affected</span>
            <span>Notes</span>
          </div>
          <div class="tr cols-16-1-14">
            <span>Interim report preparation</span>
            <span>All condensed statements</span>
            <span>Coordinated with No. 38, 39, and 40 for consolidation, cash flow, and tax matters</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s11">
      <span class="num">11</span>
      <h2>Related Standards</h2>
      <span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cd span2">
        <div class="ctitle cd">Cross-reference map</div>
        <div class="td-table">
          <div class="th cols-08-2">
            <span>Standard</span>
            <span>Connection</span>
          </div>
          <div class="tr cols-08-2">
            <span>ASBJ Statement No. 33</span>
            <span>The predecessor standard this Statement reworked and replaced</span>
          </div>
          <div class="tr alt cols-08-2">
            <span>ASBJ Statement No. 38, 39, 40</span>
            <span>The coordinated companion amendments issued alongside this Statement</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-header" id="s12">
      <span class="num">12</span>
      <h2>Quick-Reference Glossary</h2>
      <span class="line"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card cn span2">
        <div class="glossary-item">
          <div class="glossary-term">Interim financial report</div>
          <div class="glossary-def">Japan's current statutory second-quarter reporting obligation for listed companies, replacing both the older quarterly and 2024 semi-annual frameworks.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="legend">
    <div class="ltitle">Financial statement key (Japan GAAP terminology)</div>
    <div class="lrow">
      <span class="badge bs">BS</span> Balance Sheet (貸借対照表)
      <span class="badge bp">P&amp;L</span> Statement of Income / Profit and Loss Statement (損益計算書)
      <span class="badge bo">Net Assets</span> 純資産の部
      <span class="badge be">SCNA</span> Statement of Changes in Net Assets (株主資本等変動計算書)
      <span class="badge bc">SCF</span> Statement of Cash Flows (キャッシュ・フロー計算書)
    </div>
  </div>

</StandardPageLayout>
